_at":"2025-11-16T19:47:46Z","updated_at":"2025-12-01T10:59:29Z","closed_at":"2025-12-01T10:55:38Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.5.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8180) - AMD Ryzen 7 7700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.11 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen adding an item to a PopupMenu with an accelerator key thought a script and connecting the `id_pressed` signal to a custom function, the function only gets called when the MenuButton was pressed from the PopupMenu instead of also emitting when its accelerator was activated.\nThe docs of `id_pressed` state \"Emitted when an item of some id is pressed or its accelerator is activated.\" which isn't happening.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a PopupMenu in a scene.\n- Give the PopupMenu the code below:\n```gdscript\nextends PopupMenu\n\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tgrab_focus.call_deferred()\n\tvar input_key := InputEventKey.new()\n\tinput_key.keycode = KEY_A\n\tadd_item(\n\t\t\"TEST\",\n\t\t0,\n\t\tinput_key.get_keycode_with_modifiers()\n\t)\n\tid_pressed.connect(_on_id_pressed)\n\n\nfunc _on_id_pressed(id: int) -> void:\n\tprint(id)\n\t\n\tif id == 0:\n\t\tprint(\"Pressed TEST\")\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[accelerator-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23570605/accelerator-mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/